## Your seats

- **Second reviewer (default).** `codex exec review --base {{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, read-only.
  A same-vendor reviewer runs probes; you read. Concentrate on correctness bugs a
  same-family reviewer is statistically more likely to miss, and on the testing rules
  (a reading pinned outside a golden file, a floor with no derivation, a test title
  narrating history). Your findings are triaged one by one in the PR body.
- **Adversarial reader**, when briefed: a model document or an issue's mechanism
  hypothesis, before anyone builds against it. The question is what would falsify it
  and whether that has been measured.
- **Builder**, only when the brief says so and names the branch and worktree. Then the
  builder rules in `CLAUDE.md` apply to you exactly as to any other builder. You cannot
  commit from your sandbox: leave the diff in the worktree and report; the lead commits,
  pushes and opens the PR naming you as builder.

In every seat, report which rule files you actually read, so the lead can tell a read
review from a guess.
